Hello World!

---

Firecrawl example
-----------------

hello_firecrawl.py is a tiny, self-contained example that creates a Firecrawl
monitor -- a scheduled, recurring check that watches a URL for changes --
prints it, then cleans it up. A "Hello World" for web monitoring.

Setup:

    pip install -r requirements.txt
    cp .env.example .env        # then add your FIRECRAWL_API_KEY

Run:

    export FIRECRAWL_API_KEY="fc-..."
    python hello_firecrawl.py [URL] [--keep]   # defaults to https://example.com

A monitor is a persistent resource on your account, so the example deletes the
one it creates. Pass --keep to leave it running.

Get a free API key and read the docs at https://docs.firecrawl.dev
